  "prompt": "Make a gallery of nine ways to chart a comparison of scenarios, one row per example table from the Data Catalog: pedestrians per hour on four streets, flood damage curves, flooded streets by depth, peak depths of simulated storms, daily trips by mode, building carbon by life-cycle stage, park area in shade, bike route factors and green roof systems. Each table names its scenario in a case column. For every scenario keep its rows in a step of its own, with the case picked by a choice widget, and make that step the scenario; the 10-, 50- and 100-year storms are one scenario each across the two storm tables. Chart each table's scenarios in one Vega-Lite chart that reads each scenario's step directly and draws each scenario in its color: the pedestrians as lines with a band in a panel per street, the damage curves as one curve per damage state, the flooded streets as grouped bars with error bars, the peak depths as a strip of ticks per storm with its median, the daily trips as grouped bars by mode, the building carbon as stacked bars with their totals, the park shade as a donut per design, the bike route factors as a matrix of circles sized by weight and the green roof systems as a table. Those nine charts are not part of the standard node set, so whatever provides them needs installing first.",
